# carts/platformer -- the negative control for walkthrough.input. Hand-written, five bytes
# of it: hold Right from tick 0 and never let go.
#
# The start ledge is six tiles wide with nothing to its right, so the climber walks off it and
# drops onto the spikes. It exists to prove that the freeze at the end of a cleared run means
# something: a cleared tower holds a single frame for as long as the recording lasts, while a
# fall leaves the failure screen blinking, so its frame hash alternates in runs of 28 and 12
# ticks forever. One is a constant, the other is a square wave -- and "still climbing" is
# neither, because the clock in the HUD moves every tick.
#
#     quarp replay record carts/platformer -o <tmp>.qrpr --ticks 300 \
#         --input-file carts/platformer/replays/fall.input --every 1
0:R
